--[[
    ===========================================================================
    HOW THIS ESP WORKS  (and why it sometimes shows nothing at all)
    ===========================================================================

    This script does not hunt for enemies. It cannot. It only draws what the
    game has already sent to your computer.

    Kontra streams only the players you are allowed to see. Everyone else is
    not "hidden behind a wall" -- they are simply not in your copy of the game
    world. Their leftover models get parked about a million studs away and lose
    their name tag, so not even those leftovers say where anyone is.

    We checked the network side as well: the packet that carries players
    arrives with exactly as many entries as the characters you can already see.
    No extra hidden players inside it. Nothing to decode.

    So:
      * enemy in front of you    -> box appears
      * enemy walks behind cover -> the game stops sending him -> box vanishes
      * that is the game working as intended, not the script failing

    This is why a real "wallhack" ESP is not possible in Kontra. Any script
    that promises one is either lying or drawing something else entirely.

    What this script does instead: it remembers the last position the game
    actually sent for a target, and keeps a dim "last seen" box there for a
    few seconds. That is a memory, not x-ray vision.

    Reading the panel:
      "4 live"   boxes drawn right now
      "1 ghost"  last-seen markers still ticking down
      "5 hidden" characters the game parked away from you

    If live and ghost are 0 while hidden is high, nothing is broken.
    There is simply nothing on screen worth drawing.
]]
